Package: morganafa
Type: Package
Title: MORGANA Factor Analysis with Correlated Residuals
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R: person(given = "MORGANA",
                  family = "Developers",
                  role = c("aut", "cre"),
                  email = "noreply@example.com")
Description: Implements the MORGANA (Minimum expected bias Of Residual and
    loadinG vAlues iN sAmple estimates) methodology for exploratory and
    confirmatory factor analysis with correlated residuals (doublets). The
    package provides EREC-based doublet detection (LargestDoubletsEREC,
    DoubletsEREC), Parallel Analysis reference values for EREC thresholds
    (ParallelAnalysisEREC), the full unrestricted MORGANA estimation procedure
    (Morgana, MorganaEFA, MorganaCFA), and LOSEFER empirical fit-index
    correction (LoseferMorgana, LoseferMorganaH0). High-level wrappers
    solutionMEFA() and solutionMCFA() integrate all steps into a single call.
    The methodology is described in Ferrando, Hernandez-Dorado & Lorenzo-Seva
    (2022) <doi:10.1080/10705511.2021.2004543> and Lorenzo-Seva (2025)
    <doi:10.1080/03610918.2025.2453473>. These methods are also implemented in
    the program FACTOR (https://psico.fcep.urv.cat/utilitats/factor/); note
    that this R package was developed independently and no formal comparison
    between the outputs of the two implementations has been conducted.
